From: Playtendoh
Subject: [PATCH] PS5: no portable.ini or config folder, as getcwd ends the app there

mgba_retro_load_game loads the core's config (mCoreLoadConfig), which looks for portable.ini beside
getcwd() and then for HOME. On PS5-680 the C library's getcwd ended the app with signal 11 as a Game
Boy Color game started (rip in libc, mCoreConfigPortablePath on the stack), and the PS5 has no HOME.
As on the other consoles mGBA knows, no portable.ini; and no config folder of its own: the frontend
gives the folders a core uses (system, saves). The PC's build (LIBRETRO_HOST) is unchanged.

---
diff --git a/src/core/config.c b/src/core/config.c
index 0388c9f..a982d3e 100644
--- a/src/core/config.c
+++ b/src/core/config.c
@@ -255,6 +255,9 @@ void mCoreConfigDirectory(char* out, size_t outLength) {
 		}
 	}
 	WideCharToMultiByte(CP_UTF8, 0, wpath, -1, out, outLength, 0, 0);
+#elif defined(__PROSPERO__)
+	/* PS5: no HOME, and the frontend gives the folders a core uses: no config folder of its own */
+	out[0] = '\0';
 #elif defined(PSP2)
 	snprintf(out, outLength, "ux0:data/%s", projectName);
 	sceIoMkdir(out, 0777);
@@ -297,7 +300,8 @@ void mCoreConfigPortableIniPath(char* out, size_t outLength) {
 	}
 	WideCharToMultiByte(CP_UTF8, 0, wpath, -1, out, outLength, 0, 0);
 	StringCchCatA(out, outLength, PATH_SEP "portable.ini");
-#elif defined(PSP2) || defined(GEKKO) || defined(__SWITCH__) || defined(__3DS__)
+#elif defined(PSP2) || defined(GEKKO) || defined(__SWITCH__) || defined(__3DS__) || defined(__PROSPERO__)
+	/* PS5: its C library's getcwd ends the app (the Game Boys' first start): no portable.ini */
 	UNUSED(outLength);
 	out[0] = '\0';
 #else
